WEBVTT

00:00.031 --> 00:04.497
Viagra, how it works, the mechanism of action is it prevents the breakdown of nitric oxide?

00:04.697 --> 00:07.440
It prevents, it has no effect on nitric oxide.

00:07.460 --> 00:08.161
No effect on nitric oxide.

00:08.181 --> 00:09.883
No, it's downstream of nitric oxide.

00:09.903 --> 00:10.664
Oh, interesting.

00:10.684 --> 00:10.925
Okay.

00:10.945 --> 00:16.271
So nitric oxide, its primary target is an enzyme called soluble guanylyl cyclase.

00:16.532 --> 00:19.135
So nitric oxide binds to the metal in that enzyme.

00:19.155 --> 00:20.697
It's a metalloprotein, it's a protein.

00:21.418 --> 00:24.942
And then that enzyme creates a second messenger called cyclic GMP.

00:24.922 --> 00:29.215
Then in the body in the cell, there's an enzyme called phosphodiesterases.

00:29.235 --> 00:36.917
They degrade cyclic GMP So nitric oxide turns it on we see an increase in cyclic GMP the phosphodiesterases degrade it So it's a quick signal.

00:37.258 --> 00:47.588
Hmm, but the PD5 inhibitors the vagras prevent the breakdown of that second messenger Okay, so it function it works downstream of nitric oxide and it's a hundred percent dependent upon the production of nitric oxide

